1
00:00:01,598 --> 00:00:10,040
Service Requests & Complaints
Log a client request or complaint, route it to the right team and resolve it within the service level.

2
00:00:10,040 --> 00:00:13,280
Every request type comes from the service catalogue
Masters ▸ Service Request Catalogue

3
00:00:13,280 --> 00:00:40,400
Sign in as Priya Ramdin — Relationship Manager
Relationship manager — logs requests for her clients

4
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:44,880
Each type has its business unit, a service level in business hours and an approval flag
Statement request: 16 hours, no approval · Partial prepayment: 40 hours, needs approval

5
00:00:44,880 --> 00:00:48,360
Complaints get 120 business hours — 15 working days for a final response
Acknowledged within 1 business day, in line with FSC expectations

6
00:00:48,360 --> 00:01:00,600
Rohan Beeharry phones to ask for the last six months of statements
Service & Complaints ▸ New

7
00:01:00,600 --> 00:01:04,040
Pick the client, the business unit and the request type
The form only shows complaint fields when the type is Complaint

8
00:01:04,120 --> 00:01:08,280
Saved: the request is numbered, acknowledged and routed automatically
The client gets an acknowledgement email; Lending requests go to the Loans team

9
00:01:08,280 --> 00:01:13,480
Stage Acknowledged · Catalogue SLA 16 business hours · Needs approval: No
Owner: Yash Bholah, Loans team

10
00:01:13,480 --> 00:01:17,000
Activity: the acknowledgement email the client received
Sent automatically when the request was logged

11
00:01:20,080 --> 00:01:24,400
The Loans executive who owns the request works it
Hand-off from the RM to the Loans team

12
00:01:24,400 --> 00:01:32,400
Sign in as Yash Bholah — Loans Executive
Owner of the request — Loans team

13
00:01:32,400 --> 00:01:36,800
The board: one column per stage, from New to Closed
Drag the card when the work moves on

14
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:41,440
Statements prepared — try to mark it Resolved
A request cannot be resolved without the date it was resolved

15
00:01:41,440 --> 00:01:46,600
Blocked: the Resolved stage needs the "Resolved on" date
The card goes back to its column and the board says what is missing

16
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:57,960
Enter the date the request was resolved and save
Then go back to the board

17
00:01:57,960 --> 00:02:05,040
Resolved — the client is emailed a short satisfaction survey
One question on satisfaction (1–5), one on likelihood to recommend (0–10)

18
00:02:05,040 --> 00:02:07,560
Closed. The service level was met on time
The SLA timer stopped when the request was resolved

19
00:02:07,560 --> 00:02:11,720
Bhavish Dabee wants to prepay part of a home loan
Partial prepayment needs the business-unit head's approval

20
00:02:11,720 --> 00:02:17,080
Sign in as Priya Ramdin — Relationship Manager
The RM logs the request

21
00:02:17,080 --> 00:02:29,000
Same form, request type Partial prepayment
The catalogue marks this type as needing approval

22
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:32,480
Needs approval: Yes — the catalogue sent it to the business-unit head
An approval request is waiting in Tools ▸ Approvals

23
00:02:32,480 --> 00:02:36,720
The BD head reviews and approves the request
Tools ▸ Approvals — the requester can never approve their own request

24
00:02:36,720 --> 00:02:40,880
Sign in as Shalini Ramtohul — Head of BD & Strategic Partnerships
Head of BD — approves requests the catalogue flags

25
00:02:40,960 --> 00:02:50,600
The request waits in her Approvals inbox
Open the linked record to review it, add a comment, then Approve or Reject

26
00:02:50,600 --> 00:02:53,720
Approved: the owner is notified to go ahead
The decision and comment are kept on the request's Audit tab

27
00:02:53,720 --> 00:02:57,920
Stéphanie Montocchio writes in to complain about a fee
Anyone can log a complaint — request type Complaint

28
00:02:57,920 --> 00:03:03,240
Sign in as Priya Ramdin — Relationship Manager
The RM receives the complaint letter

29
00:03:03,240 --> 00:03:07,520
New request: the client, the business unit — and request type Complaint

30
00:03:07,520 --> 00:03:19,960
Choosing Complaint shows the complaint-handling fields
Category, root cause, final response, redress and Ombudsperson referral

31
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:25,160
Acknowledged automatically and routed to Compliance
Owner: Fatima Hossenbux, whatever the business unit · the complaints timer has started

32
00:03:25,160 --> 00:03:28,680
The client already has the complaint acknowledgement
In the client's language, with the reference number and the next steps

33
00:03:31,720 --> 00:03:35,800
Compliance owns the complaint and is notified
Signed in as the Compliance Officer

34
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:46,520
Sign in as Fatima Hossenbux — Compliance Officer
Compliance Officer — oversees the complaints register

35
00:03:46,520 --> 00:03:50,160
The SLA Board shows the complaint's timers
First response met · resolution due within 15 business days

36
00:03:50,200 --> 00:03:58,600
Compliance investigates
Move the complaint to In progress

37
00:03:58,600 --> 00:04:06,120
A statement copy is needed from the client — Awaiting client
While the client has the ball, the SLA clock is paused

38
00:04:06,120 --> 00:04:09,720
Paused: the waiting time does not count against the target
The clock restarts when the complaint moves on

39
00:04:09,760 --> 00:04:18,200
The client sent the statement — back to In progress
The fee was charged in error

40
00:04:18,200 --> 00:04:22,600
Try to resolve it straight away…

41
00:04:22,600 --> 00:04:28,560
Blocked: a complaint needs a root cause and a final response before it is resolved
And the date it was resolved

42
00:04:28,560 --> 00:04:34,680
Record the root cause and the final response sent to the client
Here: a system error applied the fee — it is refunded

43
00:04:34,680 --> 00:04:40,480
Root cause, final response, redress — and the Ombudsperson box
Tick it if the client refers the complaint to the Ombudsperson for Financial Services

44
00:04:40,520 --> 00:04:48,800
Saved — now move the complaint to Resolved

45
00:04:48,800 --> 00:04:55,880
Resolved: the timer stops and the satisfaction survey goes to the client

46
00:04:55,920 --> 00:05:02,480
Everything is on the complaint record
Final response, dates, emails and the full audit trail

47
00:05:02,480 --> 00:05:05,960
Activity: the acknowledgement and the satisfaction survey
Sent automatically — nobody had to remember

48
00:05:11,640 --> 00:05:17,200
Audit: every stage change, who made it and when
The evidence the FSC complaints register asks for

49
00:05:17,200 --> 00:05:24,600
When the client answers the survey, the scores are recorded on the request
They feed the CSAT and NPS figures on the Service dashboard

50
00:05:24,640 --> 00:05:29,938
The SLA Board: on-time compliance across requests and complaints
Tools ▸ SLA Board

51
00:05:29,938 --> 00:05:37,400
Service & Complaints
Requests and complaints are acknowledged, routed and timed by the system.
